<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg" data-parallax="0.15"><img src="/assets/img/photos/tupelo-elvis-birthplace.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/tupelo-elvis-birthplace-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/tupelo-elvis-birthplace.webp 1024w" sizes="100vw" width="1024" height="682" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li><a href="/counties-and-cities/">Counties &amp; cities</a></li><li aria-current="page">Tupelo</li></ol></nav><p class="kicker">North Mississippi</p><h1>Tupelo Tornado, Wind and Hail Claim Appraisal</h1><p class="lede">Tupelo knows tornadoes, from 1936 to 2014. If your Tupelo home or business was damaged and your carrier’s estimate won’t cover the repair, appraisal can resolve the amount.</p><div class="btns"><a class="btn btn-gold" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/talk-to-an-appraiser/">Free claim review</a></div><ul class="hero-facts"><li><small>County</small><b>Lee County</b></li><li><small>Region</small><b>North Mississippi</b></li><li><small>Inspections</small><b>On site</b></li></ul></div></section><div class="wrap cols"><article class="prose"><div class="glance">
<div><p class="glance-h">Neighborhoods &amp; areas</p><ul class="chips"><li>Downtown Tupelo</li><li>Fairpark</li><li>East Tupelo</li><li>Joyner</li><li>Mill Village</li><li>Saltillo</li></ul></div>
<div><p class="glance-h">Housing mix</p><p>Tupelo has older homes near downtown, a large stock of post-war and mid-century brick ranches, newer subdivisions on the edges of town, and commercial and manufacturing buildings tied to the furniture industry.</p></div>
<div><p class="glance-h">Storm history</p><ul class="storm-list"><li><b>Apr 5, 1936</b><span>Tupelo tornado, one of the deadliest in US history</span></li><li><b>Feb 1994</b><span>North Mississippi ice storm</span></li><li><b>Apr 28, 2014</b><span>EF3 tornado through Tupelo</span></li><li><b>Feb 2021</b><span>Winter storm and statewide freeze</span></li></ul></div>
<div><p class="glance-h">Local claim risks</p><ul class="chips chips-red"><li>Tornadoes and spring severe weather</li><li>Hail on shingle and metal roofs</li><li>Ice and tree damage in winter storms</li><li>Commercial and industrial roof losses</li></ul></div>
</div><h2>A city rebuilt by storms</h2>
<p>Tupelo is the county seat of Lee County and the commercial center of northeast Mississippi. It is known for the Elvis Presley birthplace in East Tupelo, for the Natchez Trace Parkway, and for a long run as a center of upholstered furniture manufacturing.</p>
<p>Tupelo’s mix of older neighborhoods, post-war housing, retail corridors and industrial buildings means a single storm can produce very different claims within a few blocks: a homeowner arguing over brick and decking, and a plant owner arguing over a large roof system.</p>
<p>It is also known for tornadoes. On April 5, 1936, a tornado tore through the city and became one of the deadliest in US history. Much of what was rebuilt after that storm, and the post-war neighborhoods that followed, still stands.</p>
<p>On April 28, 2014, the same day an EF4 struck Louisville in Winston County, an EF3 tornado crossed Tupelo, damaging homes, businesses and trees along its path.</p>

<h2>Where Tupelo claims come from</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Tornadoes and straight-line wind:</strong> spring storms remain the biggest single source of large claims.</li>
<li><strong>Hail:</strong> storms tracking across northeast Mississippi damage shingle and metal roofs alike.</li>
<li><strong>Ice and freeze:</strong> the February 1994 ice storm and the February 2021 winter storm both brought down limbs and burst pipes.</li>
<li><strong>Commercial losses:</strong> large low-slope and metal roofs on manufacturing, warehouse and retail buildings.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Tupelo homes and the gaps in their estimates</h2>
<p>Downtown Tupelo and the Fairpark district hold the city’s older core. East Tupelo, Joyner and the Mill Village area include older and mid-century houses on established lots. Newer subdivisions have spread outward toward Saltillo and other parts of Lee County.</p>
<p>The post-war and mid-century brick ranch is the most common house we see in Tupelo claims. On those homes, the recurring problems are:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Brick repair:</strong> estimates assume matching brick is available when the original brick has long been discontinued.</li>
<li><strong>Roof decking:</strong> older plank decking under a tornado-damaged roof is often left out of the scope.</li>
<li><strong>Code items:</strong> a re-roof or partial rebuild may trigger current code requirements that the estimate ignores.</li>
<li><strong>Interior water:</strong> rain through a tornado-damaged roof, scoped as a few ceiling stains.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Commercial and industrial property</h3>
<p>For furniture plants, warehouses and retail buildings, the disputes are larger but similar in kind: roof area, system type, and whether a section can be repaired or must be replaced. Our <a href="/our-appraisal-services/commercial-hoa-appraisal/">commercial and HOA appraisal</a> service covers those claims.</p>

<h2>Starting the process in Tupelo</h2>
<p>Before you demand appraisal, gather your policy, the carrier’s estimate, photos and any contractor bids. Our <a href="/claim-calculator-suite/appraisal-readiness-checkup/">appraisal readiness checkup</a> walks through what you need. If the gap is real, we can represent you through the appraisal clause, from the written demand to the award. See our <a href="/our-appraisal-services/tornado-wind-damage-appraisal/">tornado and wind damage appraisal</a> service for details.</p>
<p>Policy and legal deadlines keep running, so confirm yours with a Mississippi attorney.</p>
<h2>Appraisal services in Tupelo</h2>
<p>Every Mississippi Insurance Appraiser service is available in Tupelo and the rest of Lee County, including:</p>
<ul><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/appraisal-demand-representation/">Appraisal Demand Representation</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/home-insurance-appraisal/">Home Insurance Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/commercial-hoa-appraisal/">Commercial &amp; HOA Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/roof-hail-claim-appraisal/">Roof &amp; Hail Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/tornado-wind-damage-appraisal/">Tornado &amp; Wind Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/carrier-estimate-review/">Carrier Estimate Review</a></li></ul>
<h2>Tupelo claim questions</h2><div class="faqs"><details><summary>Can appraisal help with a commercial or manufacturing building in Tupelo?</summary><p>Yes, if the commercial policy has an appraisal clause and the dispute is about the amount of a covered loss. Large roof systems and multi-building sites are common subjects of commercial appraisal.</p></details><details><summary>Do you work claims outside the Tupelo city limits?</summary><p>Yes. We work claims across Lee County, including Saltillo, and throughout Mississippi.</p></details></div>
